        "id": 175887,
        "name": "Donner",
        "username": "Donner",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/{size}/1903_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-05-17T18:55:34.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Okay. &nbsp;Then I only see it going one way.</p><p>Hit all enemies for 2 sonic (3 sonic, actually, thanks to Crowbar), then whatever other target for 4 sonic. &nbsp;Each time a target is hit, a different target has to take the crowbar hit, but all targets could be hit this way with minor planning.</p><p>Then hit all allies for 1 sonic damage, allowing the same number of other targets to be hit for 2 sonic damage (or the same one multiple times if you want).</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
